#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:1
msgid "Autotuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:3
msgid ""
"`cutile::tune` searches a declared space of kernel configurations, measures "
"each candidate with `cutile::bench`'s device-event timing, and persists both "
"the trials and the winner. It is gated behind the `experimental-tune` "
"feature, and the API may change between releases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:8
msgid "cutile = { version = \"...\", features = [\"experimental-tune\"] }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:12
msgid ""
"Use a closure to tune an individual kernel, or implement `Objective` to "
"measure a whole request. The `autotune` example uses a closure: `cargo run -"
"p cutile-examples --example autotune --features experimental-tune`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:16
msgid "Declaring a space and running the search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:18
msgid ""
"A configuration is a set of named integer or string parameters; the space is "
"the list of configurations. Only `configs` and the terminal `run` are "
"required. The rest of the builder is optional: `prune` filters candidates, "
"`budget` bounds wall-clock, `log` makes the run resumable, and `require` "
"declares incumbents the search must cover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:24
msgid ""
"let configs: Vec<Config> = [16i64, 32, 64, 128]\n"
"    .into_iter()\n"
"    .map(|bn| Config::new([(\"BN\", ParamValue::Int(bn))]))\n"
"    .collect();\n"
"\n"
"let output = Autotuner::new(\"fmha_decode\")\n"
"    .configs(configs)\n"
"    .prune(|c| c.int(\"BN\").unwrap() <= pp)\n"
"    .require(vec![shipping_config])\n"
"    .budget(Duration::from_secs(300))\n"
"    .arch(\"sm_100\") // record the arch; a resume from another arch is "
"refused\n"
"    .log(\"fmha_decode.trials.jsonl\")\n"
"    .run(&stream, |stream, config| {\n"
"        // The setup closure is yours: read the config, build the kernel's\n"
"        // composed launcher for it, run it once as a correctness gate, and\n"
"        // return the closure to be timed. Err(..) records the candidate as\n"
"        // invalid and the search continues.\n"
"        let bn = config.int(\"BN\").unwrap();\n"
"        let mut launch = move |stream: &Arc<Stream>| {\n"
"            fmha_decode(out.partition([1, bn as i32]), &q, &k, &v)\n"
"                .generics(generics_for(bn))\n"
"                .sync_on(stream)\n"
"        };\n"
"        launch(&stream)?;\n"
"        Ok(launch)\n"
"    })?;\n"
"let best: Config = output.best.expect(\"a winner\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:54
msgid ""
"The two best candidates are compared in a paired A/B runoff to account for "
"clock and temperature drift. A finalist that fails setup forfeits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:57
msgid ""
"Every `require`d configuration must belong to the search space. These "
"configurations are measured first, before the budget can cut off the search. "
"The winner must match or beat each of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:61
msgid ""
"Trial logs record the tuner name and a hash of the search space. A log from "
"a different tuner or space is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:65
msgid "Measuring a full request with `Objective`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:67
msgid ""
"When the objective is end-to-end (tokens per second, request latency), the "
"library cannot own the launch. Implement `Objective` instead: `configs()` "
"exposes the space, `measure(index)` applies one candidate at engine scope "
"and returns a `Trial` built with `Trial::measured` or `Trial::invalid`, and "
"`budget_remaining()` reports what is left. `Autotuner::run_objective` then "
"provides the same trial logging, resume, and `require` coverage as the "
"closure path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:75
msgid ""
"let mut objective = EngineObjective::new(engine, configs);\n"
"let output = Autotuner::new(\"engine_prefill\")\n"
"    .arch(current_arch) // e.g. \"sm_100\"; resume refuses a foreign-arch "
"log\n"
"    .log(\"prefill.trials.jsonl\")\n"
"    .require(vec![current_default])\n"
"    .run_objective(&mut objective)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:84
msgid ""
"This path has no paired runoff: the library cannot re-time an engine "
"objective through its bench closures. `Output::best` is the best sequential "
"median. The caller can re-measure finalists together to check for drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:88
msgid ""
"Serialized `Trial` records remain compatible across cuTile upgrades. An "
"incompatible change increments the log schema version, and `TrialLog::open` "
"rejects the old schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:93
msgid "Committing winners"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:95
msgid ""
"A `tune::Record` persists winners so production loads them instead of re-"
"searching: one JSON file per kernel, written by `save` and committed next to "
"the code it tunes. The file holds a provenance header (kernel name, source "
"hash, cutile version, `tileiras` fingerprint, architecture, search-space "
"hash) and one entry per shape-class bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:101
msgid ""
"use cutile::tune::{L2Key, Record, RecordEntry, Workspace};\n"
"\n"
"// After tuning: `winner` is the winning Trial, `best` its Config\n"
"// (`output.best`), and `launcher` the kernel's composed builder applied\n"
"// with `best`'s values — the same call expression production dispatches.\n"
"let TrialState::Measured { median_ms, reps, .. } = winner.state else {\n"
"    unreachable!(\"the winner was measured\");\n"
"};\n"
"let mut record = Record::new(&workspace);\n"
"record.insert(RecordEntry {\n"
"    bucket: \"tg<=512\".into(),\n"
"    config: best,\n"
"    median_ms,\n"
"    samples: reps,\n"
"    l2_key: Some(L2Key::current(launcher.l2_cache_key()?)),\n"
"});\n"
"record.save(&path)?;\n"
"\n"
"// In production: load, verified against the running workspace.\n"
"let (record, warnings) = Record::load_verified(&path, &workspace, |entry| {\n"
"    Ok(Some(specialize_for(&entry.config)?.l2_cache_key()?))\n"
"})?;\n"
"let entry = record.get(\"tg<=512\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:127
msgid ""
"A bucket is a plain string label, matched exactly by `Record::get`; the "
"predicate that decides which bucket a runtime shape falls into lives in the "
"consumer's dispatch code, and the record only stores the label. `median_ms` "
"and `samples` are the winner's measured median latency and the number of "
"timed reps behind it — provenance for a human reading the committed file, "
"not inputs to verification. The `l2_key` is the winner's persistent-cache "
"key, computed from the composed builder without compiling or launching (`."
"l2_cache_key()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:136
msgid ""
"`load_verified` rejects a record if its kernel, architecture, source hash, "
"or search space differs from the running workspace. It also recomputes each "
"entry's cache key to check the kernel's dependencies and toolchain. Changes "
"that affect only timing produce warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:141
msgid "Warming and managing the kernel cache during sweeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:143
msgid ""
"Call `.compile()` on the same builder used for `.execute` or `.sync_on` to "
"warm the specialization that will run. `api::meta` tensors supply shape and "
"dtype without device allocation or kernel launches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:147
msgid ""
"my_module::my_kernel(api::meta::<f32>(&[64, 64]).sync()?.partition([16, "
"16]), ...)\n"
"    .generics(generics)\n"
"    .compile_options(opts)\n"
"    .compile()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/autotuning.md:154
msgid ""
"Tuning sweeps and long-running serving engines can accumulate many "
"specializations, and each cached kernel holds device memory. The in-memory "
"kernel cache is intentionally unbounded. The `unsafe` functions "
"`clear_kernel_cache()`, `evict_kernel(&key)`, and `retain_kernels(pred)` in "
"`cutile::tile_kernel` are available without any Cargo feature. They remove "
"entries, releasing each module's device memory when its last holder drops. "
"These functions are `unsafe`: synchronize every stream that may still be "
"running a cached kernel before evicting it. Between tuning trials or while a "
"serving engine is idle, callers can evict and then reload the needed "
"specializations. The autotuning API in `cutile::tune` still requires "
"`experimental-tune`."
msgstr ""
